      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Opting out of the struggle doesn't erase the hardship, but finding value outside of just \"grand\" achievements offers a healthier way to survive the pain of disappointment. Dignity lies in honoring your own unique path rather than forcing yourself into a mold you don't fit, even if it means your career feels modest. Sometimes, choosing to experience life with its small moments of meaning is an act of greater strength than burning out in a pursuit that brings you only frustration.",
